    {
      "question_id": 11,
      "question": "Which factors should be considered when choosing a chunk size?",
      "type": "multi_hop",
      "tags": [
        "list",
        "spans_pages",
        "project_relevant"
      ],
      "expected": "answerable",
      "trace_id": "79cd21823524",
      "action": "answered",
      "refused": false,
      "answer": "When deciding on a chunk size, consider:\n\n1. **Task’s preference** – the granularity needed for the downstream task (e.g., QA prefers short chunks ~128 tokens; summarization prefers longer chunks ~512 tokens).  \n2. **Encoder’s preference** – the maximum input length and performance of the embedding model (e.g., sentence‑transformer works best on single sentences, text‑embedding‑ada‑002 handles longer texts, BERT‑based models typically cap at 512 tokens).  \n3. **Query’s preference** – the length of user queries should align with the chunk size so that the amount of context in chunks matches that in queries (short‑phrase databases may not serve long‑document queries).  \n\nThese three factors together guide the choice of chunk size for a given RAG scenario.",
